          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "where-the-list-came-from",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "How the map compares with an earlier city series"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Mayor’s Office of Immigrant Affairs launched the Immigrant Enclave Illustration Series on April 17, 2023. In its "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://www.nyc.gov/assets/immigrants/downloads/pdf/digital-spread-12-31-2025-moia-impact.pdf",
                    "newWindow": true,
                    "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "end-of-tenure report"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " covering through December 31, 2025, the office states that 23 illustrations were published. “Little Italy” does not appear in the 85-page report."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Five names appear on the map but nowhere in that report: Little Egypt, Little Odessa, Little Palestine, Little Poland and Little Senegal. The map therefore includes five names not found in the report."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "the-two-criteria",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Two reported criteria"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Two source accounts describe different criteria for why a neighborhood might appear on the map. Neither appears in a published selection rule."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In a July 9, 2026 "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/policy/immigration/4641977/mamdani-map-nyc-immigrant-outrage-italian-community/",
                    "newWindow": true,
                    "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "Washington Examiner article"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", a city spokesperson said the map highlights neighborhoods with substantial foreign-born populations. This describes a demographic criterion based on current population."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://www.theblaze.com/news/wheres-little-italy-mamdanis-immigrant-enclave-map-sparks-backlash",
                    "newWindow": true,
                    "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "The Blaze"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " quoted people who described a neighborhood’s history of immigrant settlement as a basis for inclusion. This describes a heritage criterion that does not depend on the current foreign-born share."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The two criteria ask different questions. A neighborhood can meet either, both or neither; the evidence does not establish that either criterion was the rule used to make the map."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "the-published-threshold",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A separate Department of City Planning threshold"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Department of City Planning’s "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://www.nyc.gov/assets/planning/newest-new-yorkers-2026/Ch3.html",
                    "newWindow": true,
                    "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "The Newest New Yorkers 2026, Chapter 3"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " defines a “major immigrant neighborhood” for that report as one whose foreign-born density exceeds the city average, using a 40 percent threshold. It records SoHo-Little Italy at 30.5 percent."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The report scopes that definition to its own chapter. No source in this collection connects the threshold to the map, so the threshold is not treated here as an explanation for Little Italy’s absence."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "section",
            "id": "what-happened-next",
            "heading": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "What happened next"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "On July 10, 2026, "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "link",
                    "href": "https://www.amny.com/news/little-italy-mamdani-immigrant-map-backlash/",
                    "newWindow": true,
                    "accessibleNewWindowText": "opens in a new tab",
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "text",
                        "text": "amNewYork"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " reported that the mayor’s team had updated the map. At the same press conference, the mayor said the map had been created by the prior administration in 2023 and said future changes would include adding Little Italy."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Checked on August 20, the known map file was unchanged from archived captures taken before the July reporting. The page that had carried the map redirected to the program index, while the image file was still served. No amended map was located."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
